NOTE: each (pool_segments, thread_count, rep) cell ran in its OWN freshly-spawned OS process (subprocess-per-arm isolation), eliminating the registry-slot-reuse bug that invalidated R25-5's RSS axis. Every arm hard-asserted resolved cap == requested cap AND config_conflicts_delta == 0 before its number was trusted (see each child's own output above). Median is the reported figure; (min..max) across 3 reps shows the spread. RSS/commit are process-wide deltas on a shared Windows host (noisy point estimates) but the cap/conflicts self-checks are exact.
